{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 6.4% a year from $38.5 billion in FY2016 to $67.6 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F201]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was cyclical rather than smooth: a 22.4% drop in FY2020 to $41.7 billion [F5][D198], then a 22.1% rebound in FY2021 to $51.0 billion [F6][D251]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 decline came from lower sales volume on weaker end-user demand and dealer inventory reductions across all three primary segments [P59]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2023 was the margin peak, with operating margin up 6.0pp to 19.3% on favorable price realization and higher volume [F28][D370][P31]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 reversed part of that, operating margin falling 3.7pp to 16.5% as unfavorable manufacturing costs, largely tariffs, and price realization offset volume [F30][D476][P9]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Power & Energy is now the largest segment at 47.6% of revenue, up from 41.8% in FY2023, and added 5.2pp of FY2025 growth [D753][D757][D759]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Power Generation alone grew 32.5% in FY2025 and contributed 3.9pp, while Construction Industries fell 1.6% and subtracted 0.6pp [D894][D895][D765][D766]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Total sales rose 4.3% to $67.6 billion on higher sales volume of $3.389 billion, partly offset by unfavorable price realization of $817 million [F10][D463][P13]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew far faster than revenue over the window, at a 28.6% CAGR against 6.4%, but fell 14.7% in FY2025 [F202][F201][D464]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS fell 14.7% in FY2025, matching the net income decline, as the diluted share count fell 3.5% [D467][D465][D483]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 operating margin of 16.5% sits above the 14.3% window median but below the 20.2% FY2024 high [F30][D1123][D1122]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cost of revenue took 4.2pp off the FY2025 margin, while SG&A and R&D were roughly neutral [D490][D492][D491]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The cost-of-revenue drag reflects unfavorable manufacturing costs of $2.148 billion, largely higher tariffs [P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin fell 3.5pp to 13.1%, a smaller drop than operating margin, as other income of $892 million cushioned the decline [F50][D477][X110]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The effective tax rate rose to 24.0% from 19.7%, working against net margin [D449][D396]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $11.7 billion was 1.32x net income in FY2025, above the 0.96x free-cash-flow-to-net-income median [F80][F40][D450][D1135]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow fell 11.2% to $8.9 billion, a 13.2% margin against a 11.9% window median [F100][D469][D447][D1129]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Capex rose 41.9% to $2.8 billion, lifting capex to 1.25x D&A from 0.92x, as investing outflows grew on higher capital expenditures [F90][D470][D452][D399][P3]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Machinery operating cash flow still rose on lower working capital requirements and lower cash taxes, partly offset by lower profit [P4]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt widened to $26.2 billion in FY2025 from $24.9 billion, as total debt grew 14.1% to $36.2 billion against $10.0 billion of cash [D456][D403][D485][D455][F140]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash of -38.8% of revenue ranks at the 43rd percentile of seven industrials peers, against a peer median of -35.6% [D457][D1151][D1152]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $5.2 billion plus dividends of $2.7 billion used 89.0% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count fell 3.5% [X140][X150][D459][D483]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 43.5% is the highest of six peers, against a 23.3% peer median [D462][D1155][D1156]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt has now risen two years running, from $22.1 billion in FY2023 to $26.2 billion in FY2025, while debt funded buybacks and higher capex [D350][D456][D485]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue fell 3.4% in FY2024 to $64.8 billion on lower equipment sales to end users, a one-year dip that FY2025's 4.3% growth reversed [F9][D410][P22][D463]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net income for FY2021 to FY2025 in the table is proxy-sourced and rounded, differing from the 10-K by up to 0.06%, so the 10-K figures should be used where precision matters [R3][F40][X20]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Segment revenue members overlap, summing to 219% of consolidated revenue in FY2025, so segment lines should not be added together [R6]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin: a FY2026 print below the 14.3% window median would confirm the tariff-driven compression, while a recovery toward the 20.2% FY2024 high would reverse it [D1123][D1122]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex: FY2026 capital expenditures above the FY2025 level of $2.8 billion would keep free cash flow below the 13.2% margin and pressure net debt [F90][D447]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash: a further widening beyond -38.8% of revenue would extend the two-year deterioration in the balance sheet [D457][D456]."}
  ]}
]}
